<title>EGYPT: Yield falls on Egyptian six-month T-bills.</title>
<headline>Yield falls on Egyptian six-month T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Egyptian 182-day treasury bills fell to 10.258 percent from 10.259 percent at the previous auction on September 2.</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Egypt announced the following details (values in pounds, previous week in brackets):</p>
<p>Maturity date: Mar 11, 1997 (Mar 2, 1997)</p>
<p>Average yield: 10.258 percent (10.259)</p>
<p>Value of bids accepted: 739.550 milion (629.625 million)</p>
<p>Value of bids: 851.550 million (752.325 million)</p>
<p>Range accepted: 9.999-10.284 percent (10.101-10.284)</p>
<p>Range of bids: 9.999-10.600 percent (10.101-10.600)</p>
<p>Number of bids accepted: 115 (202)</p>
<p>Number of bids: 122 (212)</p>
<p>($1 = 3.40 pounds)</p>
<p>-- Cairo reporting unit +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
